# Module architecture audit (mandatory before done)

Documentation and README checkboxes are **not** sufficient. Before you finish work on **`module/`**, **`packages/orpc/src/orpc/procedures/`**, or thin app **`page.tsx`** routes:

```bash
pnpm audit:module-architecture
```

- Exit **0** required — CI fails on **NEW** violation ids vs **`scripts/audit-module-architecture-baseline.json`**.
- After fixing known debt, shrink baseline: **`node scripts/audit-module-architecture.mjs --write-baseline`** and commit the JSON in the same PR.
- Local burn-down: **`node scripts/audit-module-architecture.mjs --strict`**.

Rules enforced: outbound **`serviceResponseSchema(...).parse`** on controllers; no **`z.unknown()`** oRPC inputs; **`@modules/*`** or dual **`@module/*`** imports in procedures; **`unwrapTeam*`** only in legacy transport allowlist; thin Studio pages.

See [docs/tooling.md](../docs/tooling.md), [docs/gaps/agent-meta.md](../docs/gaps/agent-meta.md), [docs/new-feature-checklist.md](../docs/new-feature-checklist.md).
